{"shortDescription":"Asia's diesel markets eased for a second straight session on Tuesday, with refining margins and cash premiums hovering at one-week lows, as traders assessed October supply fundamentals.Some end-October sales by northeast Asian refiners were done in discounted territory of more than $1 a barrel, com…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Asia's diesel markets eased for a second straight session on Tuesday, with refining margins and cash premiums hovering at one-week lows, as traders assessed October supply fundamentals."]},{"type":"p","children":["Some end-October sales by northeast Asian refiners were done in discounted territory of more than $1 a barrel, compared with first-half October shipments at $3-4 a barrel."]},{"type":"p","children":["Traders were watching out for China export volumes soon, though there is still no confirmation on how much volumes will be allotted to oil majors for sales yet. Last week, at least two oil majors had sold off first-half October cargoes using their allotment for September."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meanwhile the east-west price spread hovered near discounts of $160-$170 per metric ton."]},{"type":"p","children":["Refining margins (GO10SGCKMc1) eased further to around $72.6 a barrel, still hovering at one-week lows, reflecting slightly weaker trading sentiment in the region."]},{"type":"p","children":["Cash differentials (GO10-SIN-DIF) fell, tracking the easing October-November timespreads, against a backdrop of thin spot trading activity on window."]},{"type":"p","children":["October sales for jet fuel were still ongoing from some refiners, with negotiations underway."]},{"type":"p","children":["Regrade (JETREG10SGMc1) widened further to discounts of $5 a barrel, with traders expecting the recent widening to encourage refiners to switch to more diesel production instead."]},{"type":"p","children":["SINGAPORE CASH DEALS"]},{"type":"p","children":["- No deal for jet fuel or gasoil"]},{"type":"p","children":["INVENTORIES"]},{"type":"p","children":["- US crude oil and distillate inventories were expected to have fallen last week, while gasoline stockpiles likely increased, a preliminary Reuters poll showed on Monday."]},{"type":"p","children":["REFINERY NEWS"]},{"type":"p","children":["- Russia's major Moscow refinery, owned by Gazprom Neft, has halted crude oil processing after fires broke out at its primary crude distillation units following a Ukrainian drone attack on September 20, three industry sources said."]},{"type":"p","children":["- The restart of key units at ExxonMobil's 275,000-barrel-per-day (bpd) refinery in Joliet, Illinois, was in progress one week after plant-wide shutdown due to power outage, consultancy Wood Mackenzie said on Monday."]},{"type":"p","children":["NEWS"]},{"type":"p","children":["- Namibia has selected TotalEnergies bidding group to supply the country's bulk diesel and petrol needs for a three-month period from November to January, energy minister Modestus Amutse said late on Monday."]},{"type":"p","children":["- Russia sharply increased diesel exports to Central Asian countries in August despite a ban on supplies to most foreign markets, traders said on Monday, citing recovering output."]},{"type":"p","children":["- Saudi Aramco loaded about 14 million barrels of crude oil on seven supertankers inside the Mideast Gulf on Sunday, data from TankerTrackers.com showed, as the kingdom increased loadings from Gulf export terminals after an attack disrupted shipments via its east-west pipeline to the Red Sea."]},{"type":"p","children":["PRICES"]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["MIDDLE DISTILLATES"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]}]},{"type":"table-row","child